<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35268" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-nĕcessārĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Very necessary</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tempus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 5, 21, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 4, 4, 11, § 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Very closely connected</i> with one: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amicus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Fl. 6, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					de Or. 2, 50, 202</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pro homine intimo ac mihi pernecessario,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fam. 13, 69</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">meus familiaris et Leptae nostri familiarissimi
					pernecessarius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 9, 13, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">meos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 13, 40</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
